.168.100.101 \"for host in {target_hosts}; do ssh $host \"sudo -u {username} {sudo_command}\"; done\""], "synthesizedSolution": "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \"for host in {target_hosts}; do ssh $host \"id -u {username} &>/dev/null || useradd -m -s /bin/bash -c ''Service account for {service_name}'' {username}\"; done\"\nssh root@192.168.100.101 \"for host in {target_hosts}; do ssh $host \"echo ''{username} ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: {sudo_command}'' > /etc/sudoers.d/99-{username}\"; done\"\nssh root@192.168.100.101 \"for host in {target_hosts}; do ssh $host \"chmod 440 /etc/sudoers.d/99-{username}\"; done\"\nssh root@192.168.100.101 \"for host in {target_hosts}; do ssh $host \"visudo -c\"; done\"\nssh root@192.168.100.101 \"for host in {target_hosts}; do ssh $host \"sudo -l -U {username}\"; done\"\nssh root@192.168.100.101 \"for host in {target_hosts}; do ssh $host \"sudo -u {username} {sudo_command}\"; done\""}, "kbArticleReference": "KB_NEW"}') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO "AgentApproval" ("confidenceScore", "timestamp", "details", "entityType", "summary", "id", "status", "proposedAction", "type", "entityId") VALUES ('APPR-7563', 'EXECUTION', '4443c459-64a4-4b58-b33c-aa48d4a21f76', 'Incident', 'Live diagnostics reveal the argocd namespace is active with all pods running, but argocd-applicationset-controller shows 8 restarts (last 6m33s ago) and argocd-server shows 1 restart (35m ago). This indicates instability in the applicationset controller and potential API server connectivity issues. The ArgoCD server is exposed via NodePort (30080/30443) but ''app not working'' suggests UI inaccessibility, sync failures, or repository connectivity problems. Root cause likely involves resource constraints, configuration drift, or transient network issues affecting controller loops.', 'Execute SSH Remediation', 85.0, 'EXECUTED', '2026-08-10 05:08:38.200000', '{"model": "nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b", "kbTitle": "Master SOP: ArgoCD Application Controller and Server Health Restoration", "summary": "Live diagnostics reveal the argocd namespace is active with all pods running, but argocd-applicationset-controller shows 8 restarts (last 6m33s ago) and argocd-server shows 1 restart (35m ago). This indicates instability in the applicationset controller and potential API server connectivity issues. The ArgoCD server is exposed via NodePort (30080/30443) but ''app not working'' suggests UI inaccessibility, sync failures, or repository connectivity problems. Root cause likely involves resource constraints, configuration drift, or transient network issues affecting controller loops.", "targetCi": "control plane (192.168.100.101)", "riskLevel": "HIGH", "department": "DevOps Team", "aiReasoning": "Diagnostic evidence shows argocd-applicationset-controller with 8 restarts (high churn) and argocd-server with 1 restart, indicating instability. The ''app not working'' symptom aligns with controller restarts disrupting application reconciliation and server restarts breaking UI/API access. Restarting both deployments forces fresh controller loops and re-establishes gRPC/HTTP connections. Health endpoint checks verify liveness/readiness. RBAC check ensures controller permissions. Endpoint validation confirms service connectivity. All commands target the control plane node directly via kubectl.", "safetyChecks": [{"check": "kubectl get pods -n {namespace} -l app.kubernetes.io/part-of=argocd -o jsonpath=''{range .items[*]}{.metadata.name}{\"\\t\"}{.status.phase}{\"\\t\"}{.status.containerStatuses[0].ready}{\"\\n\"}{end}''", "passed": true}, {"check": "kubectl exec -n {namespace} deployment/argocd-server -- curl -s -o /dev/null -w \"%{http_code}\" http://localhost:8080/healthz", "passed": true}, {"check": "kubectl exec -n {namespace} deployment/argocd-repo-server -- curl -s -o /dev/null -w \"%{http_code}\" http://localhost:8081/healthz", "passed": true}, {"check": "kubectl get applications -n {namespace} --no-headers 2>/dev/null | wc -l", "passed": true}], "incidentTitle": "There is an argocd namespace in the kuberenetes cluster on control plane node. The app is not working kindly fix it.", "confidenceScore": 85, "proposedCommands": ["ssh root@192.168.100.101 \"kubectl get pods -n {namespace} -o wide\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \"kubectl describe pod -l app.kubernetes.io/name=argocd-applicationset-controller -n {namespace}\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \"kubectl logs -l app.kubernetes.io/name=argocd-applicationset-controller -n {namespace} --tail=100\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \"kubectl logs -l app.kubernetes.io/name=argocd-server -n {namespace} --tail=100\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \"kubectl rollout restart deployment/argocd-applicationset-controller -n {namespace}\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \"kubectl rollout restart deployment/argocd-server -n {namespace}\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \"kubectl rollout status deployment/argocd-applicationset-controller -n {namespace} --timeout=120s\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \"kubectl rollout status deployment/argocd-server -n {namespace} --timeout=120s\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \"kubectl get svc -n {namespace} -o wide\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \"kubectl get endpoints -n {namespace}\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \"kubectl auth can-i ''*'' ''*'' --as=system:serviceaccount:{namespace}:argocd-application-controller -n {namespace}\""], "synthesizerOutput": {"kbTitle": "Master SOP: ArgoCD Application Controller and Server Health Restoration", "draftKbId": "KB-SOP-NEW", "trendInsight": "Synthesized SOP containing 11 resolution steps starting with SSH connection.", "resolutionSteps": ["ssh root@192.168.100.101 \"kubectl get pods -n {namespace} -o wide\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \"kubectl describe pod -l app.kubernetes.io/name=argocd-applicationset-controller -n {namespace}\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \"kubectl logs -l app.kubernetes.io/name=argocd-applicationset-controller -n {namespace} --tail=100\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \"kubectl logs -l app.kubernetes.io/name=argocd-server -n {namespace} --tail=100\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \"kubectl rollout restart deployment/argocd-applicationset-controller -n {namespace}\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \"kubectl rollout restart deployment/argocd-server -n {namespace}\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \"kubectl rollout status deployment/argocd-applicationset-controller -n {namespace} --timeout=120s\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \"kubectl rollout status deployment/argocd-server -n {namespace} --timeout=120s\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \"kubectl get svc -n {namespace} -o wide\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \"kubectl get endpoints -n {namespace}\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \"kubectl auth can-i ''*'' ''*'' --as=system:serviceaccount:{namespace}:argocd-application-controller -n {namespace}\""], "synthesizedSolution": "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \"kubectl get pods -n {namespace} -o wide\"\nssh root@192.168.100.101 \"kubectl describe pod -l app.kubernetes.io/name=argocd-applicationset-controller -n {namespace}\"\nssh root@192.168.100.101 \"kubectl logs -l app.kubernetes.io/name=argocd-applicationset-controller -n {namespace} --tail=100\"\nssh root@192.168.100.101 \"kubectl logs -l app.kubernetes.io/name=argocd-server -n {namespace} --tail=100\"\nssh root@192.168.100.101 \"kubectl rollout restart deployment/argocd-applicationset-controller -n {namespace}\"\nssh root@192.168.100.101 \"kubectl rollout restart deployment/argocd-server -n {namespace}\"\nssh root@192.168.100.101 \"kubectl rollout status deployment/argocd-applicationset-controller -n {namespace} --timeout=120s\"\nssh root@192.168.100.101 \"kubectl rollout status deployment/argocd-server -n {namespace} --timeout=120s\"\nssh root@192.168.100.101 \"kubectl get svc -n {namespace} -o wide\"\nssh root@192.168.100.101 \"kubectl get endpoints -n {namespace}\"\nssh root@192.168.100.101 \"kubectl auth can-i ''*'' ''*'' --as=system:serviceaccount:{namespace}:argocd-application-controller -n {namespace}\""}, "kbArticleReference": "KB_NEW"}') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO "AgentApproval" ("confidenceScore", "timestamp", "details", "entityType", "summary", "id", "status", "proposedAction", "type", "entityId") VALUES ('APPR-6650', 'EXECUTION', 'd0dc3c6d-769d-417e-84d4-3d16d6d357ce', 'Incident', 'The diagnostic findings show ArgoCD repo-server processes running and a Python port proxy listening on port 8088, indicating ArgoCD is deployed on the control plane Kubernetes cluster. The admin password is stored in the ''argocd-initial-admin-secret'' secret in the argocd namespace. Since kubectl commands were blocked during diagnostics, remediation requires executing kubectl commands to retrieve and decode the password.', 'Execute SSH Remediation', 85.0, 'EXECUTED', '2026-08-10 05:13:51.213000', '{"model": "nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b", "kbTitle": "Master SOP: Retrieve ArgoCD Admin Credentials for Control Plane Cluster", "summary": "The diagnostic findings show ArgoCD repo-server processes running and a Python port proxy listening on port 8088, indicating ArgoCD is deployed on the control plane Kubernetes cluster. The admin password is stored in the ''argocd-initial-admin-secret'' secret in the argocd namespace. Since kubectl commands were blocked during diagnostics, remediation requires executing kubectl commands to retrieve and decode the password.", "targetCi": "control plane (192.168.100.101)", "riskLevel": "HIGH", "department": "DevOps Team", "aiReasoning": "The live diagnostics confirm ArgoCD components are running (argocd-repo-server processes) and a proxy is listening on port 8088. Standard ArgoCD installations store the initial admin password in the ''argocd-initial-admin-secret'' secret in the argocd namespace. The resolution steps retrieve this password, verify ArgoCD server pods are running, and establish a port-forward for UI access on port 8080 (alternative to the existing 8088 proxy). Safety checks validate the secret exists and pods are healthy before proceeding.", "safetyChecks": [{"check": "kubectl get secret argocd-initial-admin-secret -n argocd", "passed": true}, {"check": "kubectl get pods -n argocd | grep -E ''argocd-server|argocd-repo-server''", "passed": true}, {"check": "ss -tulpn | grep 8088", "passed": true}], "incidentTitle": "There is an Argocd application running the controlplane kuberenetes cluster. I need login details of it. ", "confidenceScore": 85, "proposedCommands": ["ssh root@192.168.100.101 \"kubectl get secret argocd-initial-admin-secret -n argocd -o jsonpath=''{.data.password}'' | base64 -d && echo\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \"kubectl get pods -n argocd -l app.kubernetes.io/name=argocd-server -o wide\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \"kubectl port-forward svc/argocd-server -n argocd 8080:443 --address=0.0.0.0 &\""], "synthesizerOutput": {"kbTitle": "Master SOP: Retrieve ArgoCD Admin Credentials for Control Plane Cluster", "draftKbId": "KB-SOP-NEW", "trendInsight": "Synthesized SOP containing 3 resolution steps starting with SSH connection.", "resolutionSteps": ["ssh root@192.168.100.101 \"kubectl get secret argocd-initial-admin-secret -n argocd -o jsonpath=''{.data.password}'' | base64 -d && echo\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \"kubectl get pods -n argocd -l app.kubernetes.io/name=argocd-server -o wide\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \"kubectl port-forward svc/argocd-server -n argocd 8080:443 --address=0.0.0.0 &\""], "synthesizedSolution": "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \"kubectl get secret argocd-initial-admin-secret -n argocd -o jsonpath=''{.data.password}'' | base64 -d && echo\"\nssh root@192.168.100.101 \"kubectl get pods -n argocd -l app.kubernetes.io/name=argocd-server -o wide\"\nssh root@192.168.100.101 \"kubectl port-forward svc/argocd-server -n argocd 8080:443 --address=0.0.0.0 &\""}, "kbArticleReference": "KB_NEW"}') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
